1
00:00:00,388 --> 00:00:01,138
(upbeat music)

2
00:00:01,222 --> 00:00:03,222
Satoru, show him
to his dorm room.

3
00:00:03,305 --> 00:00:07,264
Be sure to explain the security
arrangements to him as well.

4
00:00:09,848 --> 00:00:13,766
You're admitted,
welcome to Jujutsu Tech.

5
00:00:14,349 --> 00:00:15,682
[Yuuji] Hey, Fushiguro!

6
00:00:16,515 --> 00:00:17,432
Wow, you look all better now.

7
00:00:17,515 --> 00:00:19,235
There's lots of other
empty rooms, you know?

8
00:00:19,307 --> 00:00:22,600
Sure, but isn't it better
to have some company?

9
00:00:22,683 --> 00:00:23,475
I thought it'd be good for--

10
00:00:23,558 --> 00:00:25,016
Classes and the
missions are enough.

11
00:00:25,099 --> 00:00:27,141
This is not welcome.

12
00:00:27,225 --> 00:00:29,433
Whoa-oah, it's so
organized in here.

13
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:30,808
Back off.

14
00:00:30,892 --> 00:00:33,184
I just told you
you're not welcome!

15
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:35,392
Huh, friends already

16
00:00:35,476 --> 00:00:37,100
and together, we're
heading out tomorrow.

17
00:00:37,184 --> 00:00:41,101
We're gonna go pick up
the third and final first year.

18
00:00:42,727 --> 00:00:44,936
(whistle blows)

19
00:00:45,018 --> 00:00:47,477
[Announcer] The train bound
for Shibuya and Shinagawa

20
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,603
is now arriving on track one.

21
00:00:51,561 --> 00:00:54,228
For your safety, please
stand behind the yellow line.

22
00:00:56,353 --> 00:00:57,353
[Nobara] Saori,

23
00:00:59,103 --> 00:01:01,145
I'm finally here.

24
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:08,021
I'm in Tokyo.

25
00:01:09,271 --> 00:01:11,813
How are there only
three first years?

26
00:01:11,897 --> 00:01:12,271
That's practically nothing.

27
00:01:12,355 --> 00:01:13,355
Think about it.

28
00:01:13,438 --> 00:01:16,021
Can you honestly say
you've ever met someone else

29
00:01:16,104 --> 00:01:17,105
who sees curses?

30
00:01:17,189 --> 00:01:20,272
Huh, I guess not.

31
00:01:20,356 --> 00:01:23,981
Because jujutsu
sorcerers, they're rare.

32
00:01:24,064 --> 00:01:26,357
[Yuuji] Didn't you say I
was the third first year?

33
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,232
[Fushiguro] The others
admission was decided a while ago.

34
00:01:30,774 --> 00:01:32,690
You know what
our school is like.

35
00:01:32,774 --> 00:01:34,190
Everyone has
unique circumstances.

36
00:01:35,399 --> 00:01:37,066
Sorry for the wait.

37
00:01:37,149 --> 00:01:40,775
Oh, your uniform
made it in time.

38
00:01:40,858 --> 00:01:42,524
Yeah, it fits great.

39
00:01:42,608 --> 00:01:45,359
Though I noticed it's slightly
different from Fushiguro's.

40
00:01:45,442 --> 00:01:46,984
Mine has got a hood.

41
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:48,126
[Gojou] That's
because the uniforms

42
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:50,150
can be customized upon request.

43
00:01:50,234 --> 00:01:51,234
Huh?

44
00:01:51,317 --> 00:01:53,860
But I never put in any requests.

45
00:01:53,944 --> 00:01:56,318
You're right, I was the one
who put in the custom order.

46
00:01:56,401 --> 00:01:58,151
Huh.

47
00:01:58,985 --> 00:02:00,318
Oh, well cool.

48
00:02:00,401 --> 00:02:03,861
Be careful, Gojou has a habit
of doing that kind of stuff.

49
00:02:05,110 --> 00:02:06,295
So why are we meeting
up here in Harajuku?

50
00:02:06,319 --> 00:02:09,361
[Gojou] Because that's
what she asked for.

51
00:02:09,444 --> 00:02:11,946
[Yuuji] Yay popcorn,
I want some!

52
00:02:12,028 --> 00:02:13,153
Why hello there.

53
00:02:13,237 --> 00:02:15,028
Are you on the clock right now?

54
00:02:15,111 --> 00:02:16,528
[Woman] No, not right now.

55
00:02:16,612 --> 00:02:17,779
That's great, you see,

56
00:02:17,862 --> 00:02:19,570
I'm looking for
potential models.

57
00:02:19,654 --> 00:02:21,196
That's what I do.

58
00:02:21,279 --> 00:02:22,738
Would you be interested?

59
00:02:22,821 --> 00:02:24,404
[Woman] I'm in
a hurry right now.

60
00:02:24,488 --> 00:02:26,279
[Talent Scout] Wait,
just hear me out.

61
00:02:28,655 --> 00:02:31,113
Hey you, what about me?

62
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,072
[Talent Scout] Oh boy, her?

63
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,572
For that modeling gig.

64
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:38,822
Hey, I'm asking what
you think about me.

65
00:02:38,906 --> 00:02:41,114
Oh well, I'm in a
hurry at the moment.

66
00:02:43,657 --> 00:02:44,573
What the hell?

67
00:02:44,657 --> 00:02:46,782
Don't run, come out
and say what you think!

68
00:02:46,865 --> 00:02:49,491
Wait, she's the one we
have to go and talk to?

69
00:02:51,157 --> 00:02:53,241
This is real embarrassing.

70
00:02:53,324 --> 00:02:54,241
(scoffs) Yeah, so are you.

71
00:02:54,324 --> 00:02:56,324
Hey, we're over here!

72
00:02:57,867 --> 00:03:00,742
[Girl] Oh damn, what's
up with that blindfold?

73
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,283
Right, I'd like you to meet...

74
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,826
Nobara Kugisaki.

75
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,576
You should be honored, boys.

76
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,868
I'm your group's girl.

77
00:03:12,493 --> 00:03:15,953
(Opening Theme Music)

78
00:03:31,078 --> 00:03:34,913
(singing in Japanese)

79
00:04:42,795 --> 00:04:43,836
Stare...

80
00:04:47,754 --> 00:04:49,796
I'm Yuuji Itadori from Sendai.

81
00:04:50,963 --> 00:04:52,045
Fushiguro.

82
00:04:53,671 --> 00:04:55,379
He looks like a potato.

83
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:58,380
He's definitely the type that
ate his own boogers as a kid.

84
00:04:58,463 --> 00:05:00,713
And just his name?

85
00:05:00,797 --> 00:05:02,338
I can't stand
high-and-mighty dudes.

86
00:05:02,421 --> 00:05:06,631
I bet he likes setting
oil-slicked seagulls on fire.

87
00:05:08,172 --> 00:05:09,482
(groans) This is what
I get to work with?

88
00:05:09,506 --> 00:05:11,965
Great, just my luck.

89
00:05:12,047 --> 00:05:13,381
She took one look and sighed.

90
00:05:13,464 --> 00:05:14,547
That can't be good.

91
00:05:14,631 --> 00:05:16,590
Are we going
somewhere from here?

92
00:05:16,674 --> 00:05:20,131
(chuckles) Well we do have
all three of you together.

93
00:05:20,215 --> 00:05:23,507
And since two of you kids
are from the countryside,

94
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:26,299
that means we're going to Tokyo!

95
00:05:26,383 --> 00:05:27,299
[All] Tokyo! Tokyo!

96
00:05:27,383 --> 00:05:29,383
Tokyo!

97
00:05:29,466 --> 00:05:30,383
[Both] We love Tokyo!

98
00:05:30,466 --> 00:05:31,383
-Huh?
-TDL!

99
00:05:31,466 --> 00:05:33,759
I want to go to TDL!

100
00:05:33,842 --> 00:05:35,509
Idiot! TDL's in Chiba!

101
00:05:35,592 --> 00:05:37,425
Let's go hit up
Chinatown instead!

102
00:05:37,509 --> 00:05:39,342
Chinatown's in Yokohama, dummy!

103
00:05:39,425 --> 00:05:41,259
Well Yokohama's part of Tokyo!

104
00:05:41,342 --> 00:05:43,510
How do you not know
that? Look at a map!

105
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:46,802
If you quiet down, I'll
announce our destination.

106
00:05:46,885 --> 00:05:47,885
Roppongi!

107
00:05:50,051 --> 00:05:51,427
[Both] Roppongi?

108
00:05:55,052 --> 00:05:56,386
[Fushiguro]
There's a curse here.

109
00:05:56,469 --> 00:05:58,344
-You liar!
-You liar!

110
00:05:58,427 --> 00:05:59,654
-This isn't Roppongi!
-It's a cruel move

111
00:05:59,678 --> 00:06:02,345
to toy with country folk!

112
00:06:02,428 --> 00:06:05,136
[Gojou] There's a
big cemetery nearby.

113
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:06,971
That, plus an
abandoned building,

114
00:06:07,053 --> 00:06:07,887
and you've got a curse.

115
00:06:07,971 --> 00:06:10,429
So they pop up more
often around graves.

116
00:06:10,513 --> 00:06:11,805
Huh?

117
00:06:11,888 --> 00:06:13,763
It's not the cemetery itself.

118
00:06:13,846 --> 00:06:15,572
It's the fact that people
associate cemeteries

119
00:06:15,596 --> 00:06:18,179
with fear and uneasiness.

120
00:06:18,263 --> 00:06:20,681
Right, it was the same
for schools, too, wasn't it?

121
00:06:20,764 --> 00:06:21,847
Wait hold up here.

122
00:06:21,931 --> 00:06:23,091
He didn't even know that yet?

123
00:06:23,555 --> 00:06:24,597
To be honest...

124
00:06:27,097 --> 00:06:28,015
(gulps)

125
00:06:28,098 --> 00:06:31,056
He swallowed a
special-grade cursed object?

126
00:06:31,139 --> 00:06:32,056
Gross!

127
00:06:32,139 --> 00:06:33,449
That's so unsanitary and
disgusting I wanna hurl.

128
00:06:33,473 --> 00:06:35,723
No way, no way, no way!

129
00:06:35,807 --> 00:06:36,723
That's not nice.

130
00:06:36,807 --> 00:06:37,849
I agree with her.

131
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:40,557
I want to know what the
three of you are capable of.

132
00:06:40,641 --> 00:06:42,516
Just think of this as
a kind of field test.

133
00:06:42,599 --> 00:06:44,849
Nobara, Yuuji,

134
00:06:44,933 --> 00:06:47,475
you go exorcize the
curse inside that building.

135
00:06:47,558 --> 00:06:48,809
(Nobara grunts)

136
00:06:48,892 --> 00:06:50,058
Hold on.

137
00:06:50,141 --> 00:06:52,684
I thought only curses
could exorcize curses.

138
00:06:52,767 --> 00:06:55,225
I can't use jujutsu yet.

139
00:06:55,309 --> 00:06:58,059
If you look at it, you're
basically half a curse already.

140
00:06:58,142 --> 00:06:59,685
Cursed energy flows
through your body.

141
00:06:59,768 --> 00:07:01,518
Although, controlling
that energy

142
00:07:01,601 --> 00:07:03,559
isn't something you
can learn overnight.

143
00:07:03,643 --> 00:07:05,019
So you use this.

144
00:07:08,185 --> 00:07:09,686
The Slaughter Demon.

145
00:07:09,769 --> 00:07:11,602
A weapon imbued
with cursed energy.

146
00:07:11,686 --> 00:07:13,435
So it'll work on curses too.

147
00:07:14,311 --> 00:07:15,520
Ugh, how lame.

148
00:07:18,812 --> 00:07:20,228
[Gojou] Oh, one more thing.

149
00:07:20,311 --> 00:07:22,938
-Huh?
-Don't let Sukuna out, okay?

150
00:07:23,771 --> 00:07:27,896
If you use him, you'll get
rid of all curses in that radius,

151
00:07:27,980 --> 00:07:29,562
but anyone nearby
will get dragged in.

152
00:07:29,646 --> 00:07:31,562
You got it. I won't let him out.

153
00:07:33,605 --> 00:07:34,522
(Nobara grunts)

154
00:07:34,605 --> 00:07:36,063
Would you hurry it up?

155
00:07:36,146 --> 00:07:38,230
-All right, all right.
-Have fun!

156
00:07:45,731 --> 00:07:47,606
(door creaking)

157
00:07:49,815 --> 00:07:52,274
I think I'll go in too.

158
00:07:52,357 --> 00:07:53,565
Don't push yourself.

159
00:07:53,649 --> 00:07:54,482
You're still
recovering, you know.

160
00:07:54,565 --> 00:07:57,399
[Fushiguro] But someone
needs to keep an eye

161
00:07:57,482 --> 00:07:57,816
on Itadori, right?

162
00:07:57,899 --> 00:07:59,942
[Gojou] True.

163
00:08:00,025 --> 00:08:03,108
But the one we're testing
this time around is Nobara.

164
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:04,900
What a pain in my ass.

165
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,525
I come all the way to Tokyo

166
00:08:06,608 --> 00:08:08,776
and I still have to
deal with dumb curses.

167
00:08:08,859 --> 00:08:10,067
Huh?

168
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:11,651
You didn't come
here to exorcize them?

169
00:08:11,734 --> 00:08:13,109
Let's save some time.

170
00:08:13,192 --> 00:08:14,484
You and I should split up.

171
00:08:14,567 --> 00:08:16,543
I'll start from the top and
investigate floor by floor.

172
00:08:16,567 --> 00:08:18,902
You start from the bottom.

173
00:08:18,986 --> 00:08:21,610
Let's knock this out and
grab some sushi in Ginza.

174
00:08:21,694 --> 00:08:22,819
Hold on a minute.

175
00:08:22,902 --> 00:08:24,819
Let's take this seriously.

176
00:08:24,902 --> 00:08:26,945
Curses are dangerous, you know.

177
00:08:27,028 --> 00:08:28,695
(Nobara grunting)

178
00:08:28,778 --> 00:08:29,695
(Yuuji screams)

179
00:08:29,778 --> 00:08:30,611
I don't wanna hear
it from someone

180
00:08:30,695 --> 00:08:33,194
who last week was
a clueless normie!

181
00:08:33,278 --> 00:08:36,445
Now get moving! (grunts)

182
00:08:36,529 --> 00:08:39,320
You're an out of control roller
coaster of emotions today!

183
00:08:39,404 --> 00:08:41,153
[Nobara] This is why
girls don't like you!

184
00:08:41,237 --> 00:08:42,797
How do you know
they don't like me, huh?

185
00:08:43,862 --> 00:08:46,571
Are you even popular
enough to talk?

186
00:08:46,655 --> 00:08:47,655
Bitch.

187
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:50,822
Huh?

188
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:53,780
(splashing)

189
00:08:53,863 --> 00:08:56,531
(upbeat music)

190
00:08:59,239 --> 00:09:01,239
Do you need a receipt?

191
00:09:04,490 --> 00:09:05,532
It's a curse!

192
00:09:06,115 --> 00:09:07,615
(curse warbling)

193
00:09:07,699 --> 00:09:10,865
(screaming)

194
00:09:21,116 --> 00:09:23,492
(grunting)

195
00:09:27,284 --> 00:09:28,325
Hmm-mm.

196
00:09:29,117 --> 00:09:29,659
Have I got moves or what?

197
00:09:29,742 --> 00:09:31,827
(guts splashing)

198
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:32,952
That Yuuji.

199
00:09:34,368 --> 00:09:36,410
Some screws are loose.

200
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:37,827
He's fearless.

201
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,995
These things take the
form of terrifying creatures

202
00:09:40,077 --> 00:09:41,327
and try to kill him.

203
00:09:42,577 --> 00:09:45,119
Yet the guy has
no hesitation at all.

204
00:09:46,869 --> 00:09:47,744
And he doesn't
have the familiarity

205
00:09:47,828 --> 00:09:50,161
with curses that you have.

206
00:09:51,495 --> 00:09:52,287
We're talking about a boy

207
00:09:52,370 --> 00:09:54,745
who used to live a
normal high school life.

208
00:09:54,829 --> 00:09:58,413
By now, you've seen
plenty of jujutsu sorcerers,

209
00:09:58,496 --> 00:09:59,788
some talented.

210
00:09:59,871 --> 00:10:01,413
And you've seen them give up

211
00:10:01,496 --> 00:10:04,162
'cause they couldn't conquer
their fear or disgust, right?

212
00:10:06,746 --> 00:10:09,706
So today's about seeing if
she's crazy enough for this.

213
00:10:11,163 --> 00:10:13,539
(sighs) Hey. Whaddup, curse?

214
00:10:20,123 --> 00:10:22,248
Yeah you, mannequin
in the center.

215
00:10:22,331 --> 00:10:24,206
You actually think
you're hidden there?

216
00:10:27,082 --> 00:10:28,000
Fine then.

217
00:10:28,082 --> 00:10:29,374
I'll do this from here.

218
00:10:30,791 --> 00:10:32,582
But Kugisaki has
experience, right?

219
00:10:32,666 --> 00:10:34,457
So it's a little
late for that now.

220
00:10:34,541 --> 00:10:36,792
As we know, curses are
born from human minds.

221
00:10:36,875 --> 00:10:38,667
So their strength and numbers

222
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:41,667
grow in proportion
to the population.

223
00:10:43,375 --> 00:10:46,418
(light upbeat music)

224
00:10:48,209 --> 00:10:50,793
(Nobara grunts)

225
00:11:00,919 --> 00:11:03,753
Do you think Nobara understands

226
00:11:03,837 --> 00:11:06,837
Tokyo curses are
on a different level

227
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,628
than those in the countryside?

228
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:13,087
(upbeat music)

229
00:11:16,046 --> 00:11:18,713
(upbeat music)

230
00:11:27,588 --> 00:11:29,714
Curses are born
from human minds.

231
00:11:30,715 --> 00:11:32,381
So their strength and numbers

232
00:11:32,464 --> 00:11:34,715
grow in proportion
to the population.

233
00:11:34,798 --> 00:11:37,423
Tokyo curses are
on a different level

234
00:11:37,506 --> 00:11:39,215
than those in the countryside.

235
00:11:46,841 --> 00:11:49,842
You know, you might
wanna pull those out,

236
00:11:50,925 --> 00:11:53,758
(snaps fingers)

237
00:11:55,258 --> 00:11:57,551
or my cursed energy
will flow into you.

238
00:11:59,509 --> 00:12:02,259
(curse shatters)

239
00:12:05,634 --> 00:12:10,343
Nailed it. (giggles)

240
00:12:19,261 --> 00:12:20,261
A kid?

241
00:12:21,261 --> 00:12:21,886
Must've snuck in here to play

242
00:12:21,970 --> 00:12:24,762
but ran into the curse instead.

243
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:30,429
Hey, it's alright now.

244
00:12:30,512 --> 00:12:31,512
Come on out.

245
00:12:32,971 --> 00:12:34,430
(kid whimpers)

246
00:12:34,513 --> 00:12:35,430
(Nobara sighs)

247
00:12:35,513 --> 00:12:37,972
(clears throat)

248
00:12:39,179 --> 00:12:41,471
Guess he's intimidated
by my beauty.

249
00:12:41,555 --> 00:12:42,596
It happens a lot.

250
00:12:43,514 --> 00:12:44,931
-I'll call Itadori.
-Wait!

251
00:12:47,514 --> 00:12:49,222
Don't leave me here! (screams)

252
00:12:49,306 --> 00:12:51,973
(curse warbling)

253
00:12:52,056 --> 00:12:53,932
(kid screaming)

254
00:12:55,974 --> 00:12:57,932
(curse laughing)

255
00:13:08,308 --> 00:13:09,766
[Nobara] It took him hostage?

256
00:13:11,350 --> 00:13:13,517
This curse has intelligence?

257
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,726
When I say level,

258
00:13:14,809 --> 00:13:17,559
I don't just mean the amount
of cursed energy they have.

259
00:13:18,642 --> 00:13:19,267
It's their cunning.

260
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:21,310
Monsters that have gained wisdom

261
00:13:21,393 --> 00:13:22,977
will often force cruel
choices upon you.

262
00:13:25,351 --> 00:13:28,101
Where the weight of human
lives hang in the balance.

263
00:13:28,184 --> 00:13:29,936
Damn it, damn it, damn it!

264
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,020
Damn it!

265
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,020
This curse isn't
even all that strong!

266
00:13:36,352 --> 00:13:37,269
Grade 4.

267
00:13:37,352 --> 00:13:39,228
Maybe even less,
like a low grade 3!

268
00:13:40,021 --> 00:13:40,937
(kid whimpers)

269
00:13:41,021 --> 00:13:42,312
But it's aware of that!

270
00:13:43,353 --> 00:13:45,395
That's why it chose
to take a hostage!

271
00:13:48,146 --> 00:13:49,396
Calm yourself down.

272
00:13:51,104 --> 00:13:53,396
If I die, the boy dies, too.

273
00:13:55,187 --> 00:13:57,689
But if he dies, I won't die.

274
00:13:59,897 --> 00:14:02,897
Logically speaking, it's
better if at least I survive.

275
00:14:02,981 --> 00:14:05,023
I mean, right?

276
00:14:12,273 --> 00:14:13,398
I'm unarmed now.

277
00:14:14,148 --> 00:14:15,190
Let the boy go.

278
00:14:16,649 --> 00:14:19,441
(curse laughing)

279
00:14:22,441 --> 00:14:23,608
I'm such an idiot.

280
00:14:24,442 --> 00:14:26,400
It's not letting
go of him at all.

281
00:14:27,442 --> 00:14:30,275
(curse laughing)

282
00:14:31,692 --> 00:14:35,234
Poor Saori, I wish I could've
seen her one last time.

283
00:14:36,651 --> 00:14:39,609
(loud thud)

284
00:14:39,693 --> 00:14:40,693
Huh? I missed?

285
00:14:50,444 --> 00:14:51,570
(loud thud)

286
00:14:51,653 --> 00:14:54,570
-(curse warbling)
-(upbeat music)

287
00:14:54,653 --> 00:14:54,945
You okay, bud?

288
00:14:55,029 --> 00:14:57,111
Uh-huh.

289
00:14:57,194 --> 00:14:58,945
(curse warbling)

290
00:14:59,029 --> 00:15:01,112
It's getting away!

291
00:15:01,195 --> 00:15:02,362
No he's not!

292
00:15:02,446 --> 00:15:04,112
-Itadori, give me that arm!
-Huh?

293
00:15:06,112 --> 00:15:08,154
(curse warbling)

294
00:15:08,237 --> 00:15:09,530
-I'll handle it.
-Hold on.

295
00:15:11,488 --> 00:15:13,447
-A straw doll?
-Creepy.

296
00:15:17,697 --> 00:15:18,906
Straw Doll Technique:

297
00:15:21,156 --> 00:15:22,073
Resonance!

298
00:15:22,156 --> 00:15:25,781
(curse warbling)

299
00:15:30,074 --> 00:15:30,991
Oh good.

300
00:15:31,074 --> 00:15:33,365
All right, she's crazy.

301
00:15:39,283 --> 00:15:40,283
We beat it.

302
00:15:43,533 --> 00:15:46,367
(soft piano music)

303
00:15:51,743 --> 00:15:54,367
(truck beeping)

304
00:15:57,702 --> 00:16:00,493
When I was in first grade,

305
00:16:00,577 --> 00:16:02,744
Saori moved to our
village from Tokyo.

306
00:16:07,369 --> 00:16:09,119
Huh?

307
00:16:15,162 --> 00:16:18,162
She was as cute as a doll

308
00:16:20,203 --> 00:16:21,203
and as kind as a nun.

309
00:16:31,121 --> 00:16:35,622
Yet Saori was ostracized
by the villagers.

310
00:16:39,122 --> 00:16:42,165
"She thinks us country
folk are dumb," they said,

311
00:16:42,248 --> 00:16:45,373
they got swept up
in their own paranoia.

312
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:47,790
And in the end,

313
00:16:51,249 --> 00:16:52,249
they drove her out.

314
00:16:56,416 --> 00:16:58,291
Calling it sickening
wouldn't cover it.

315
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:07,500
She brought all these homemade
sweets I'd never heard of,

316
00:17:07,584 --> 00:17:09,752
"The ones from the
bakery are even better,"

317
00:17:09,835 --> 00:17:11,793
she'd smile as she
treated me to them.

318
00:17:16,460 --> 00:17:19,294
If I had stayed in
that village, then I...

319
00:17:21,794 --> 00:17:23,419
[Yuuji] This is why I told you!

320
00:17:23,502 --> 00:17:24,294
I said it's dangerous
to go alone

321
00:17:24,377 --> 00:17:26,920
and you need to
take it seriously!

322
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:29,420
Except you never said it
was dangerous to go alone!

323
00:17:29,503 --> 00:17:31,087
I, wait, I didn't?

324
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:32,754
And dude, what
have you been eating

325
00:17:32,837 --> 00:17:35,545
that lets you punch through
a wall with your bare hand?

326
00:17:35,628 --> 00:17:37,129
[Yuuji] It wasn't
reinforced concrete!

327
00:17:37,212 --> 00:17:38,212
[Nobara] So?

328
00:17:38,296 --> 00:17:39,880
Most people couldn't
punch through that!

329
00:17:41,296 --> 00:17:42,838
You really don't think so?

330
00:17:43,296 --> 00:17:45,422
You know, you've asked
me a ton of questions

331
00:17:45,505 --> 00:17:47,213
but I've got one for you.

332
00:17:47,297 --> 00:17:49,797
Like why did you
come to Jujutsu Tech?

333
00:17:49,881 --> 00:17:51,172
Why am I here?

334
00:17:51,255 --> 00:17:53,797
Because the countryside sucked!

335
00:17:53,881 --> 00:17:56,214
And I always wanted
to live in Tokyo!

336
00:17:56,298 --> 00:17:58,548
(Yuuji screams)

337
00:17:58,631 --> 00:18:01,049
This was the only
way a poor girl like me

338
00:18:01,131 --> 00:18:03,382
could move to the city
without worrying about money!

339
00:18:03,466 --> 00:18:06,466
You'd risk your life
to save a few bucks?

340
00:18:09,924 --> 00:18:10,966
I would.

341
00:18:15,342 --> 00:18:17,467
Since it means
being true to myself.

342
00:18:18,717 --> 00:18:20,258
(soft music)

343
00:18:20,342 --> 00:18:24,259
If I had stayed in that
village, I'd be as good as dead.

344
00:18:35,135 --> 00:18:36,344
Saori, I made it to Tokyo.

345
00:18:43,428 --> 00:18:44,762
If we ever meet here,

346
00:18:45,928 --> 00:18:48,219
take me to that
bakery you mentioned.

347
00:18:53,554 --> 00:18:57,679
So as far as that goes,
I'm grateful to you, too.

348
00:18:57,763 --> 00:18:59,138
If you hadn't been here,

349
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,847
and he or I had been killed,

350
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:02,597
the future wouldn't
be so bright.

351
00:19:03,930 --> 00:19:04,972
So thanks.

352
00:19:06,097 --> 00:19:08,681
Well, I guess we've
all got our own reasons

353
00:19:08,765 --> 00:19:09,806
for being here.

354
00:19:10,765 --> 00:19:11,681
Drop it!

355
00:19:11,765 --> 00:19:12,306
I've given you
my thanks already.

356
00:19:12,389 --> 00:19:15,015
We're even now! (giggles)

357
00:19:15,098 --> 00:19:16,098
What is wrong with her?

358
00:19:17,766 --> 00:19:19,640
I live over there!

359
00:19:19,724 --> 00:19:20,724
Thanks again!

360
00:19:23,724 --> 00:19:26,683
Did you know I get into a
bad mood when I'm hangry?

361
00:19:26,767 --> 00:19:29,059
[Yuuji] When are you
not in a bad mood?

362
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,391
[Gojou] Hey there!

363
00:19:31,475 --> 00:19:32,266
Huh?

364
00:19:32,350 --> 00:19:35,018
We made sure the kid got home.

365
00:19:36,976 --> 00:19:39,309
Now how about we grab some food?

366
00:19:39,392 --> 00:19:43,684
-A juicy steak.
-Sushi!

367
00:19:43,768 --> 00:19:44,518
Just leave it all to me!

368
00:19:44,602 --> 00:19:46,352
Megumi, you in?

369
00:19:49,143 --> 00:19:50,185
Huh?

370
00:19:50,268 --> 00:19:51,268
Okay, let's go.

371
00:19:54,478 --> 00:19:58,436
[Nobara] Oh, I forgot about
my biggest haul of the day.

372
00:19:58,519 --> 00:20:00,728
Hey, you, go fetch my things.

373
00:20:00,811 --> 00:20:02,354
[Yuuji] Huh? Why
should I do that?

374
00:20:02,437 --> 00:20:04,479
I thought we were even now.

375
00:20:04,562 --> 00:20:07,063
[Nobara] We won thanks
to my cursed energy.

376
00:20:07,145 --> 00:20:07,896
Got a problem with that?

377
00:20:07,979 --> 00:20:09,645
[Yuuji] What about
my raw strength?

378
00:20:09,729 --> 00:20:11,228
[Nobara] That freak
strength you get

379
00:20:11,313 --> 00:20:11,938
from eating weird shit?

380
00:20:12,022 --> 00:20:13,938
[Yuuji] It's not just from that!

381
00:20:14,022 --> 00:20:15,022
Right, Fushiguro?

382
00:20:16,313 --> 00:20:17,414
Huh? Fushiguro,
what's the matter?

383
00:20:17,438 --> 00:20:19,396
Nothing.

384
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,939
He's pouting 'cause
he didn't get to fight.

385
00:20:22,023 --> 00:20:23,023
Poor little baby.

386
00:20:24,023 --> 00:20:24,564
(Fushiguro grunts)

387
00:20:24,647 --> 00:20:28,065
(Yuuji laughs)

388
00:20:30,523 --> 00:20:34,024
[Kiyokata] Log: July 2018.

389
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:37,648
West Tokyo City, Eishuu
Juvenile Detention Center.

390
00:20:40,191 --> 00:20:42,232
In the sky above
the exercise yard.

391
00:20:44,399 --> 00:20:48,109
Hey, what is that?

392
00:20:50,026 --> 00:20:51,192
What's what?

393
00:20:51,275 --> 00:20:55,150
[Kiyokata] Unnamed Apparition
of Potential Special Grade.

394
00:20:55,233 --> 00:20:56,609
Its curse womb was witnessed

395
00:20:56,692 --> 00:20:58,485
by several
non-jujutsu sorcerers.

396
00:21:00,610 --> 00:21:02,818
[Teen] That up there!
Looks like an egg.

397
00:21:02,902 --> 00:21:04,651
[Tadashi] What are
you talking about?

398
00:21:06,110 --> 00:21:07,819
[Kiyokata] Due to
its emergency nature,

399
00:21:07,903 --> 00:21:11,444
three Jujutsu Tech first-years
were dispatched to the scene.

400
00:21:11,527 --> 00:21:14,277
And one of them died.

401
00:21:16,071 --> 00:21:21,071
(Closing Theme Music)

402
00:22:45,621 --> 00:22:46,955
[All] Juju Stroll.

403
00:22:48,163 --> 00:22:50,039
[Nobara] I'm going
with paper, Itadori.

404
00:22:51,163 --> 00:22:53,246
[Both] Rock, paper, scissors!

405
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:54,246
-(Yuuji grunts)
-Yeah!

406
00:22:54,330 --> 00:22:57,123
I guess we can go to
the sushi place in Ginza.

407
00:22:57,206 --> 00:22:58,247
Ginza, yeah!

408
00:22:59,373 --> 00:23:00,956
I want revolving sushi!

409
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:01,831
(Nobara grunts)

410
00:23:01,915 --> 00:23:04,123
[Nobara] Itadori,
you're such a (grunts),

411
00:23:04,206 --> 00:23:05,487
Fushiguro, say something to him!

412
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:07,374
If we're going, we should
get something good.

413
00:23:07,457 --> 00:23:08,665
Since Gojou's paying.

414
00:23:08,749 --> 00:23:10,415
Revolving sushi's its own thing,

415
00:23:10,499 --> 00:23:12,957
like how yakisoba and
instant yakisoba are different!

416
00:23:13,041 --> 00:23:14,917
Yeah but I wanna
eat big girl sushi.

417
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,200
[Yuuji] Sushi's a boring meal!

418
00:23:16,249 --> 00:23:17,917
Revolving sushi's an experience!

419
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,458
Like a theme park! Or TDL!

420
00:23:19,541 --> 00:23:21,333
And you said you
were from the country,

421
00:23:21,416 --> 00:23:23,959
so have you ever even been
to a revolving sushi place?

422
00:23:24,043 --> 00:23:24,959
My favorite is Sushi Go,

423
00:23:25,043 --> 00:23:28,167
but I'd go with Splendid
Sushi for a first-timer.

424
00:23:28,250 --> 00:23:28,709
You totally get it!

425
00:23:28,793 --> 00:23:31,292
Hey, cool your jets.

426
00:23:31,376 --> 00:23:33,168
Kugisaki, listen closely.

427
00:23:33,251 --> 00:23:34,585
At Splendid Sushi,

428
00:23:34,668 --> 00:23:37,127
the sushi is delivered
to you on a bullet train.

429
00:23:37,210 --> 00:23:38,251
What?!

430
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:41,335
Driver, this girl's never
had revolving sushi.

431
00:23:41,418 --> 00:23:43,669
Take us to Splendid Sushi
with the huge-ass parking lot!

432
00:23:44,711 --> 00:23:48,878
(upbeat dramatic music)

